WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.280
The Presidential Commission on the Supreme&nbsp;
Court, which held its final meeting in early

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.960
December 2021, was designed to provide&nbsp;
analysis of possible reforms of the Court.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.400
AEI's Adam White was one of the commissioners. The&nbsp;
commission did not take a position on one proposal

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.320
favored by many progressives: expanding the court's&nbsp;
membership. What do Americans think?

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.784
Americans opposed Franklin Roosevelt's court packing plan&nbsp;
and polls today show more opposition than support — though

00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:37.760
responses vary. A September Monmouth University&nbsp;
poll found 58% opposed to expanding the court with

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:44.320
36% in favor. The July Marquette Law School&nbsp;
poll also found more opposition than support.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.960
April polls by Morning Consult and Ipsos/Reuters&nbsp;
found more opposition than support — 46% to 26% in

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:57.200
the former, and 42% to 38% in the latter. In each&nbsp;
case, Democrats were more in favor of expansion

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:04.320
than Republicans. The Reuters/Ipsos poll also found&nbsp;
that 63% supported term or age limits for

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.289
the Justices while 22% were opposed.

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:13.409
Do&nbsp;you think the Supreme Court should be reformed?
And if so, how? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.418
Also let us know what other topics you'd like
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:17.418 --> 00:01:22.400
and be sure to like and&nbsp;subscribe
for more research and videos from AEI.

